[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m model_response Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m problem
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m Given the sequence $ A $ of length $ N $. The $ i $ item in $ A $ is $ A_i $. You can do the following for this sequence:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m * $ 1 \ leq i \ leq N --Choose the integer i that is 1 $. Swap the value of $ A_i $ with the value of $ A_ {i + 1} $.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m Find the minimum number of operations required to make $ A $ a sequence of bumps.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m A sequence of length $ N $ that satisfies the following conditions is defined as a sequence of irregularities.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m * For any $ i $ that satisfies $ 1 <i <N $, ​​$ A_ {i + 1}, A_ {i --1}> A_i $ or $ A_ {i + 1}, A_ {i --1} <A_i Satisfy $.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m Intuitively, increase, decrease, increase ... (decrease, like $ 1, \ 10, \ 2, \ 30, \ \ dots (10, \ 1, \ 30, \ 2, \ \ dots) $ It is a sequence that repeats increase, decrease ...).
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m output
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218555)[0m 
