[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m model_response Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m Recently Adaltik discovered japanese crosswords. Japanese crossword is a picture, represented as a table sized a × b squares, and each square is colored white or black. There are integers to the left of the rows and to the top of the columns, encrypting the corresponding row or column. The number of integers represents how many groups of black squares there are in corresponding row or column, and the integers themselves represents the number of consecutive black squares in corresponding group (you can find more detailed explanation in Wikipedia https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_crossword).
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m Adaltik decided that the general case of japanese crossword is too complicated and drew a row consisting of n squares (e.g. japanese crossword sized 1 × n), which he wants to encrypt in the same way as in japanese crossword. [Image] The example of encrypting of a single row of japanese crossword. 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m Help Adaltik find the numbers encrypting the row he drew.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m -----Input-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m The first line of the input contains a single integer n (1 ≤ n ≤ 100) — the length of the row. The second line of the input contains a single string consisting of n characters 'B' or 'W', ('B' corresponds to black square, 'W' — to white square in the row that Adaltik drew).
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m -----Output-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m The first line should contain a single integer k — the number of integers encrypting the row, e.g. the number of groups of black squares in the row.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m The second line should contain k integers, encrypting the row, e.g. corresponding to sizes of groups of consecutive black squares in the order from left to right.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m -----Examples-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m Input
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 3
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m BBW
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m Output
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 2 
