[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m Sum all the numbers of the array (in F# and Haskell you get a list) except the highest and the lowest element (the value, not the index!).
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m (The highest/lowest element is respectively only one element at each edge, even if there are more than one with the same value!)
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m Example:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m ```
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m { 6, 2, 1, 8, 10 } => 16
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m { 1, 1, 11, 2, 3 } => 6
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m ```
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m If array is empty, null or None, or if only 1 Element exists, return 0.
