[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m model_response Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m Snuke is buying a bicycle.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m The bicycle of his choice does not come with a bell, so he has to buy one separately.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m He has very high awareness of safety, and decides to buy two bells, one for each hand.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m The store sells three kinds of bells for the price of a, b and c yen (the currency of Japan), respectively.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m Find the minimum total price of two different bells.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m -----Constraints-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m  - 1 \leq a,b,c \leq 10000
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m  - a, b and c are integers.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m -----Input-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m Input is given from Standard Input in the following format:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m a b c
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m -----Output-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m Print the minimum total price of two different bells.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m -----Sample Input-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 700 600 780
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m -----Sample Output-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 1300
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m  - Buying a 700-yen bell and a 600-yen bell costs 1300 yen.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m  - Buying a 700-yen bell and a 780-yen bell costs 1480 yen.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m  - Buying a 600-yen bell and a 780-yen bell costs 1380 yen.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m The minimum among these is 1300 yen.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m The input will be stdin and you should print your solution to stdout
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m afterremove def solve():
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m     # Read input from stdin and store it in variables
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m     a, b, c = map(int, input().split()) 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m     # Return the minimum total price of two different bells 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m     # Calculate the minimum total price of two different bells
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m     ans = min(a + b, a + c, b + c) 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m     # Return the minimum total price 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m     return ans 
