[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m You'll have a function called "**sortEmotions**" that will return an array of **emotions** sorted. It has two parameters, the first parameter called "**arr**" will expect an array of **emotions** where an **emotion** will be one of the following:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m - **:D** -> Super Happy
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m - **:)** -> Happy
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m - **:|** -> Normal
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m - **:(** -> Sad
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m - **T\_T** -> Super Sad
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m Example of the array:``[ 'T_T', ':D', ':|', ':)', ':(' ]``
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m And the second parameter is called "**order**", if this parameter is **true** then the order of the emotions will be descending (from **Super Happy** to **Super Sad**) if it's **false** then it will be ascending (from **Super Sad** to **Super Happy**)
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m Example if **order** is true with the above array: ``[ ':D', ':)', ':|', ':(', 'T_T' ]``
