[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m model_responsemodel_response  Let's call an undirected graph of n vertices p-interesting, if the following conditions fulfill:   the graph contains exactly 2n + p edges;  the graph doesn't contain self-loops and multiple edges;  for any integer k (1 ≤ k ≤ n), any subgraph consisting of k vertices contains at most 2k + p edges. 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m A subgraph of a graph is some set of the graph vertices and some set of the graph edges. At that, the set of edges must meet the condition: both ends of each edge from the set must belong to the chosen set of vertices. 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m Your task is to find a p-interesting graph consisting of n vertices.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m -----Input-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m The first line contains a single integer t (1 ≤ t ≤ 5) — the number of tests in the input. Next t lines each contains two space-separated integers: n, p (5 ≤ n ≤ 24; p ≥ 0; $2 n + p \leq \frac{n(n - 1)}{2}$) — the number of vertices in the graph and the interest value for the appropriate test. 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m It is guaranteed that the required graph exists.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m -----Output-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m For each of the t tests print 2n + p lines containing the description of the edges of a p-interesting graph: the i-th line must contain two space-separated integers a_{i}, b_{i} (1 ≤ a_{i}, b_{i} ≤ n; a_{i} ≠ b_{i}) — two vertices, connected by an edge in the resulting graph. Consider the graph vertices numbered with integers from 1 to n. 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m Print the answers to the tests in the order the tests occur in the input. If there are multiple solutions, you can print any of them.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218551)[0m -----Examples-----
