[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Evi has N integers a_1,a_2,..,a_N. His objective is to have N equal integers by transforming some of them.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m He may transform each integer at most once. Transforming an integer x into another integer y costs him (x-y)^2 dollars. Even if a_i=a_j (i≠j), he has to pay the cost separately for transforming each of them (See Sample 2).
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
