[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m xaxxxxa
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 3
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m aaabaa
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 6
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Note
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m In the first example, it's enough to erase any four of the "x"s. The answer is 3 since that is the maximum number of characters that can remain.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m In the second example, we don't need to erase any characters.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m The input will be given via stdin and the output should be printed to stdout by your code.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
