[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m model_response Read problems statements in Mandarin Chinese  and Russian. 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Andy and Bob are the only two delivery men of Pizza-chef store. Today, the store received N orders. 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m It's known that the amount of tips may be different when handled by different delivery man. 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m More specifically, if Andy takes the i^{th} order, he would be tipped A_{i} dollars and if Bob takes this order, 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m the tip would be B_{i} dollars. 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m They decided that they would distribute the orders among themselves to maximize the total tip money. One order will be handled by only
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m one person. Also, due to time constraints Andy cannot take more than X orders and Bob cannot take more than 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Y orders. It is guaranteed that X + Y is greater than or equal to N, which means that all the orders can be handled 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m by either Andy or Bob.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 	
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Please find out the maximum possible amount of total tip money after processing all the orders.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m ------ Input ------ 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m The first line contains three integers N, X, Y.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m The second line contains N integers. The i^{th} integer represents A_{i}.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m The third line contains N integers. The i^{th} integer represents B_{i}.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m ------ Output ------ 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Print a single integer representing the maximum tip money they would receive.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m ------ Constraints ------ 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m All test:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m $1 ≤ N ≤ 10^{5}$
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m $1 ≤ X, Y ≤ N; X + Y ≥ N $
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m $1 ≤ A_{i}, B_{i} ≤ 10^{4}$
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 10 points:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m $1 ≤ N ≤ 20$
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 30 points:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m $1 ≤ N ≤ 5000$
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 60 points:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m $1 ≤ N ≤ 10^{5}$
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m ----- Sample Input 1 ------ 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 5 3 3
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 1 2 3 4 5
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 5 4 3 2 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m ----- Sample Output 1 ------ 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 21
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m ----- explanation 1 ------ 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Bob will take the first three orders (or the first two) and Andy will take the rest (of course).
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m afterremove def solve():
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     n,x,y = map(int,input().split())
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     a = list(map(int,input().split()))
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     b = list(map(int,input().split()))
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     ans = 0
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     for i in range(n):
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m         if x > 0:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m             ans += a[i]
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m             x -= 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m         elif y > 0:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m             ans += b[i]
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m             y -= 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     return ans
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
