[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m model_response Consider the number triangle below, in which each number is equal to the number above plus the number to the left. If there is no number above, assume it's a `0`.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m The triangle has `5` rows and the sum of the last row is `sum([1,4,9,14,14]) = 42`.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m You will be given an integer `n` and your task will be to return the sum of the last row of a triangle of `n` rows. 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m In the example above:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m More examples in test cases. Good luck!
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m ```if:javascript
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m ### Note
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m This kata uses native arbitrary precision integer numbers ( `BigInt`, `1n` ).  
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Unfortunately, the testing framework and even native `JSON` do not fully support them yet.  
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m `console.log(1n)` and `(1n).toString()` work and can be used for debugging.  
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m We apologise for the inconvenience.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m ```
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m afterremove def solve():
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     n = 5
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     # Create a list to store the triangle
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     triangle = [[0] * i for i in range(1, n + 1)] 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     # Fill in the triangle with values 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     for i in range(n):
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m         for j in range(i + 1): 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m             # Add the values from the previous row 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m             if i == 0:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m                 triangle[i][j] = 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m             elif j == 0 or j == i:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m                 triangle[i][j] = triangle[i - 1][j - 1] + triangle[i - 1][j]
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m             else:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m                 triangle[i][j] = triangle[i - 1][j - 1] + triangle[i - 1][j] 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m   
