[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m model_response Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Chef Jessie has a lot of recipes with her (N). She often remembered the starting few characters of the recipe and forgot the rest. As all the great chefs do, Jessie also numbered the recipes depending on the priority. So, given the list of recipes along with their priorities answer Jessie’s queries.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Jessie’s queries are as follows:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m She gives you the first few characters of a recipe; you have to print the complete recipe with the highest priority.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Note:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Every recipe has a unique priority
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m First line contains an integer N - the number of recipes.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Followed by N strings Si along with an integer each Vi.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Si stands for the recipe and Vi for the priority.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m It is followed by an integer Q - the number of queries.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Followed by Q strings Qi.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Each string Si, Qi contain only lowercase Latin alphabets ('a' - 'z') and '-'.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Q – lines, each contain the answer for each of the query.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m If for a query no recipe matches print "NO". (Without quotes)
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Constraints:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 0 <= N <= 1000
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 0 <= Q <= 1000
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m -10^9 <= Vi <= 10^9
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 1 <= |Si| <= 1000 (length of Si)
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 1 <= |Qi| <= 1000 (length of Qi)
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m -----Example-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Input:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 4
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m flour-with-eggs 100
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m chicken-ham -10
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m flour-without-eggs 200
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m fish-with-pepper 1100
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 6
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m f
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m flour-with
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m flour-with-
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m c
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m fl
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m chik
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Output:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m fish-with-pepper
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m flour-without-eggs
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m flour-with-eggs
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m chicken-ham
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m flour-without-eggs
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m NO
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m The input will be stdin and you should print your solution to stdout
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Now solve the problem and return the code.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m afterremove def solve():
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     # Read the number of recipes
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     n = int(input()) 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     # Initialize an empty list to store recipes
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     recipes = [] 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     # Iterate through each recipe
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     for i in range(n): 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m         # Read the recipe and priority
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m         recipe, priority = input().split() 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m         # Append the recipe to the list
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m         recipes.append((priority, recipe)) 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     # Sort the recipes based on priority
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     recipes.sort() 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     # Read the number of queries
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m     for _ in range(int(input())): 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m         # Read the query string
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m         query = input() 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m         # Iterate through the sorted recipes
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m         for priority, recipe in recipes: 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m             # Check if the query matches the recipe
