[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m model_response A string is a palindrome if it reads the same from the left to the right and from the right to the left. For example, the strings "kek", "abacaba", "r" and "papicipap" are palindromes, while the strings "abb" and "iq" are not.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m A substring $s[l \ldots r]$ ($1 \leq l \leq r \leq |s|$) of a string $s = s_{1}s_{2} \ldots s_{|s|}$ is the string $s_{l}s_{l + 1} \ldots s_{r}$.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Anna does not like palindromes, so she makes her friends call her Ann. She also changes all the words she reads in a similar way. Namely, each word $s$ is changed into its longest substring that is not a palindrome. If all the substrings of $s$ are palindromes, she skips the word at all.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Some time ago Ann read the word $s$. What is the word she changed it into?
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m The first line contains a non-empty string $s$ with length at most $50$ characters, containing lowercase English letters only.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m If there is such a substring in $s$ that is not a palindrome, print the maximum length of such a substring. Otherwise print $0$.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m Note that there can be multiple longest substrings that are not palindromes, but their length is unique.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m -----Examples-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m mew
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 3
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m wuffuw
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 5
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m qqqqqqqq
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 0
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m -----Note-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m "mew" is not a palindrome, so the longest substring of it that is not a palindrome, is the string "mew" itself. Thus, the answer for the first example is $3$.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m The string "uffuw" is one of the longest non-palindrome substrings (of length $5$) of the string "wuffuw", so the answer for the second example is $5$.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m All substrings of the string "qqqqqqqq" consist of equal characters so they are palindromes. This way, there are no non-palindrome substrings. Thus, the answer for the third example is $0$.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218553)[0m 
