[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m model_response Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m For a given weighted graph G(V, E) and a source r, find the source shortest path to each vertex from the source (SSSP: Single Source Shortest Path).
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Constraints
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m * 1 ≤ |V| ≤ 100000
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m * 0 ≤ di ≤ 10000
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m * 0 ≤ |E| ≤ 500000
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m * There are no parallel edges
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m * There are no self-loops
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m An edge-weighted graph G (V, E) and the source r.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m |V| |E| r
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m s0 t0 d0
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m s1 t1 d1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m :
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m s|E|-1 t|E|-1 d|E|-1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m |V| is the number of vertices and |E| is the number of edges in G. The graph vertices are named with the numbers 0, 1,..., |V|-1 respectively. r is the source of the graph.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m si and ti represent source and target vertices of i-th edge (directed) and di represents the cost of the i-th edge.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Print the costs of SSSP in the following format.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m c0
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m c1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m :
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m c|V|-1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m The output consists of |V| lines. Print the cost of the shortest path from the source r to each vertex 0, 1, ... |V|-1 in order. If there is no path from the source to a vertex, print INF.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Examples
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 4 5 0
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 0 1 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 0 2 4
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 1 2 2
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 2 3 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 1 3 5
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 0
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 3
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 4
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 4 6 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 0 1 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 0 2 4
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 2 0 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 1 2 2
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 3 1 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 3 2 5
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 3
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 0
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 2
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m INF
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m The input will be stdin and you should print your solution to stdout
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Now solve the problem and return the code.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m afterremove def solve():
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     # Read the number of vertices and edges
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     V, E, r = map(int, input().split()) 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     # Create an empty adjacency list 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     # Create an adjacency list for the graph
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     adj = [[] for _ in range(V)] 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     # Iterate through each edge 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     for _ in range(E): 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m         # Read the source and target vertices 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m         s, t, d = map(int, input().split()) 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m         # Add the edge to the adjacency list 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m         adj[s].append((t, d)) 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     # Create a dictionary to store the distances 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     # Initialize the distance array with infinity
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     dist = [float('inf')] * V 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     # Set the distance of the source vertex to 0 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     dist[r] = 0 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     # Iterate until all vertices are visited 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     # Do the relaxation operation
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     for _ in range(V): 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m         # Iterate through all the vertices 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m         for u, (v, w) in enumerate(adj): 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m             # Update the distance if a shorter path is found 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m             if dist[v] < dist[u] + w:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m                 dist[v] = dist[u] + w 
