[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m model_response Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m For a given weighted graph G(V, E) and a source r, find the source shortest path to each vertex from the source (SSSP: Single Source Shortest Path).
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Constraints
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m * 1 ≤ |V| ≤ 100000
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m * 0 ≤ di ≤ 10000
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m * 0 ≤ |E| ≤ 500000
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m * There are no parallel edges
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m * There are no self-loops
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m An edge-weighted graph G (V, E) and the source r.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m |V| |E| r
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m s0 t0 d0
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m s1 t1 d1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m :
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m s|E|-1 t|E|-1 d|E|-1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m |V| is the number of vertices and |E| is the number of edges in G. The graph vertices are named with the numbers 0, 1,..., |V|-1 respectively. r is the source of the graph.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m si and ti represent source and target vertices of i-th edge (directed) and di represents the cost of the i-th edge.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Print the costs of SSSP in the following format.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m c0
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m c1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m :
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m c|V|-1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m The output consists of |V| lines. Print the cost of the shortest path from the source r to each vertex 0, 1, ... |V|-1 in order. If there is no path from the source to a vertex, print INF.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Examples
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 4 5 0
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 0 1 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 0 2 4
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 1 2 2
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 2 3 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 1 3 5
