[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m model_response Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m We have a bingo card with a 3\times3 grid. The square at the i-th row from the top and the j-th column from the left contains the number A_{i, j}.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m The MC will choose N numbers, b_1, b_2, \cdots, b_N. If our bingo sheet contains some of those numbers, we will mark them on our sheet.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Determine whether we will have a bingo when the N numbers are chosen, that is, the sheet will contain three marked numbers in a row, column, or diagonal.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m -----Constraints-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - All values in input are integers.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - 1 \leq A_{i, j} \leq 100
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - A_{i_1, j_1} \neq A_{i_2, j_2} ((i_1, j_1) \neq (i_2, j_2))
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - 1 \leq N \leq 10
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - 1 \leq b_i \leq 100
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - b_i \neq b_j (i \neq j)
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Input is given from Standard Input in the following format:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m A_{1, 1} A_{1, 2} A_{1, 3}
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m A_{2, 1} A_{2, 2} A_{2, 3}
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m A_{3, 1} A_{3, 2} A_{3, 3}
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m N
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m b_1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m \vdots
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m b_N
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m If we will have a bingo, print Yes; otherwise, print No.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m -----Sample Input-----
