[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m model_response Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m You are given an integer N. Among the integers between 1 and N (inclusive), how many Shichi-Go-San numbers (literally "Seven-Five-Three numbers") are there?
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Here, a Shichi-Go-San number is a positive integer that satisfies the following condition:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - When the number is written in base ten, each of the digits 7, 5 and 3 appears at least once, and the other digits never appear.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m -----Constraints-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - 1 \leq N < 10^9
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - N is an integer.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Input is given from Standard Input in the following format:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m N
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Print the number of the Shichi-Go-San numbers between 1 and N (inclusive).
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m -----Sample Input-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 575
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m -----Sample Output-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 4
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m There are four Shichi-Go-San numbers not greater than 575: 357, 375, 537 and 573.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m The input will be stdin and you should print your solution to stdout
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Now solve the problem and return the code.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m afterremove def solve():
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     N = int(input()) 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     # Initialize count to 0 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     count = 0 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     # Iterate through each number from 1 to N 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m     for i in range(1, N+1): 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m         # Convert the number to string 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m         digits = str(i) 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m         # Check if all digits are present 
