[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m model_response Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m For integers b (b \geq 2) and n (n \geq 1), let the function f(b,n) be defined as follows:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - f(b,n) = n, when n < b
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - f(b,n) = f(b,\,{\rm floor}(n / b)) + (n \ {\rm mod} \ b), when n \geq b
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Here, {\rm floor}(n / b) denotes the largest integer not exceeding n / b,
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m and n \ {\rm mod} \ b denotes the remainder of n divided by b.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Less formally, f(b,n) is equal to the sum of the digits of n written in base b.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m For example, the following hold:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - f(10,\,87654)=8+7+6+5+4=30
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - f(100,\,87654)=8+76+54=138
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m You are given integers n and s.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Determine if there exists an integer b (b \geq 2) such that f(b,n)=s.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m If the answer is positive, also find the smallest such b.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m -----Constraints-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - 1 \leq n \leq 10^{11}
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - 1 \leq s \leq 10^{11}
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m  - n,\,s are integers.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
