[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Let's define logical OR as an operation on two logical values (i. e. values that belong to the set {0, 1}) that is equal to 1 if either or both of the logical values is set to 1, otherwise it is 0. We can define logical OR of three or more logical values in the same manner:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m <image> where <image> is equal to 1 if some ai = 1, otherwise it is equal to 0.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Nam has a matrix A consisting of m rows and n columns. The rows are numbered from 1 to m, columns are numbered from 1 to n. Element at row i (1 ≤ i ≤ m) and column j (1 ≤ j ≤ n) is denoted as Aij. All elements of A are either 0 or 1. From matrix A, Nam creates another matrix B of the same size using formula:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m <image>.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m (Bij is OR of all elements in row i and column j of matrix A)
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m Nam gives you matrix B and challenges you to guess matrix A. Although Nam is smart, he could probably make a mistake while calculating matrix B, since size of A can be large.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218552)[0m The first line contains two integer m and n (1 ≤ m, n ≤ 100), number of rows and number of columns of matrices respectively.
