[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m model_response model_responsemodel_response Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m We have N gemstones labeled 1 through N.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m You can perform the following operation any number of times (possibly zero).
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m * Select a positive integer x, and smash all the gems labeled with multiples of x.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Then, for each i, if the gem labeled i remains without getting smashed, you will receive a_i yen (the currency of Japan). However, a_i may be negative, in which case you will be charged money.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m By optimally performing the operation, how much yen can you earn?
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Constraints
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m * All input values are integers.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m * 1 \leq N \leq 100
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m * |a_i| \leq 10^9
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Input is given from Standard Input in the following format:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m N
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m a_1 a_2 ... a_N
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Print the maximum amount of money that can be earned.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Examples
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
