[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m model_response Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m There are N children standing in a line from left to right. The activeness of the i-th child from the left is A_i.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m You can rearrange these children just one time in any order you like.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m When a child who originally occupies the x-th position from the left in the line moves to the y-th position from the left, that child earns A_x \times |x-y| happiness points.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Find the maximum total happiness points the children can earn.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Constraints
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m * 2 \leq N \leq 2000
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m * 1 \leq A_i \leq 10^9
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m * All values in input are integers.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Input is given from Standard Input in the following format:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m N
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m A_1 A_2 ... A_N
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Print the maximum total happiness points the children can earn.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Examples
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
