[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m model_response Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Dr. Evil kidnapped Mahmoud and Ehab in the evil land because of their performance in the Evil Olympiad in Informatics (EOI). He decided to give them some problems to let them go.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Dr. Evil is interested in sets, He has a set of n integers. Dr. Evil calls a set of integers evil if the MEX of it is exactly x. the MEX of a set of integers is the minimum non-negative integer that doesn't exist in it. For example, the MEX of the set {0, 2, 4} is 1 and the MEX of the set {1, 2, 3} is 0 .
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Dr. Evil is going to make his set evil. To do this he can perform some operations. During each operation he can add some non-negative integer to his set or erase some element from it. What is the minimal number of operations Dr. Evil has to perform to make his set evil?
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m The first line contains two integers n and x (1 ≤ n ≤ 100, 0 ≤ x ≤ 100) — the size of the set Dr. Evil owns, and the desired MEX.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m The second line contains n distinct non-negative integers not exceeding 100 that represent the set.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m The only line should contain one integer — the minimal number of operations Dr. Evil should perform.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Examples
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 5 3
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 0 4 5 6 7
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 2
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 1 0
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 0
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 5 0
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 1 2 3 4 5
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 0
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Note
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m For the first test case Dr. Evil should add 1 and 2 to the set performing 2 operations.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m For the second test case Dr. Evil should erase 0 from the set. After that, the set becomes empty, so the MEX of it is 0.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m In the third test case the set is already evil.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m afterremove def solve():
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     n, x = map(int, input().split())
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     nums = list(map(int, input().split())) 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     # Check if the set is already evil 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     nums.sort() 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     # Initialize the count of operations 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     count = 0 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     # Iterate through each number in the set 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     for i in range(n): 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m         # Check if the MEX is not found 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m         if nums[i] != i: 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m             # Increment the count of operations 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m             count += 1 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     # Return the minimum number of operations 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     if nums[n-1] != x: 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m         # Increment the count of operations 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m         count += 1 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     # Return the final count of operations 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     return count 
