[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m model_response Given is a string S. Let T be the concatenation of K copies of S. We can repeatedly perform the following operation: choose a character in T and replace it with a different character. Find the minimum number of operations required to satisfy the following condition: any two adjacent characters in T are different.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Constraints
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m * 1 \leq |S| \leq 100
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m * S consists of lowercase English letters.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m * 1 \leq K \leq 10^9
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m * K is an integer.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Input is given from Standard Input in the following format:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
