[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m model_response Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m One day, little Vasya found himself in a maze consisting of (n + 1) rooms, numbered from 1 to (n + 1). Initially, Vasya is at the first room and to get out of the maze, he needs to get to the (n + 1)-th one.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m The maze is organized as follows. Each room of the maze has two one-way portals. Let's consider room number i (1 ≤ i ≤ n), someone can use the first portal to move from it to room number (i + 1), also someone can use the second portal to move from it to room number p_{i}, where 1 ≤ p_{i} ≤ i.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m In order not to get lost, Vasya decided to act as follows.   Each time Vasya enters some room, he paints a cross on its ceiling. Initially, Vasya paints a cross at the ceiling of room 1.  Let's assume that Vasya is in room i and has already painted a cross on its ceiling. Then, if the ceiling now contains an odd number of crosses, Vasya uses the second portal (it leads to room p_{i}), otherwise Vasya uses the first portal. 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Help Vasya determine the number of times he needs to use portals to get to room (n + 1) in the end.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m The first line contains integer n (1 ≤ n ≤ 10^3) — the number of rooms. The second line contains n integers p_{i} (1 ≤ p_{i} ≤ i). Each p_{i} denotes the number of the room, that someone can reach, if he will use the second portal in the i-th room.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Print a single number — the number of portal moves the boy needs to go out of the maze. As the number can be rather large, print it modulo 1000000007 (10^9 + 7).
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 2
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 1 2
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 4
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 4
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 1 1 2 3
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 20
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 5
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 1 1 1 1 1
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 62
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m The input will be stdin and you should print your solution to stdout
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Now solve the problem and return the code.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m afterremove def solve():
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     n = int(input())
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     p = list(map(int, input().split())) 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     # Initialize the number of portal moves 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     dp = [0] * (n + 1) 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     # Initialize the starting room 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     dp[1] = 2 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     # Iterate through the rooms 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     for i in range(2, n + 1): 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m         # Calculate the number of moves for the current room 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m         dp[i] = dp[i - 1] + 1 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m         # Adjust the number of moves based on the portal 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m         if p[i - 1] > i:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m             dp[i] -= 1 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m         # Update the number of moves for the next room 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     return dp[n] 
