[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Given two integers p and k, find a polynomial f(x) with non-negative integer coefficients strictly less than k, whose remainder is p when divided by (x + k). That is, f(x) = q(x)·(x + k) + p, where q(x) is a polynomial (not necessarily with integer coefficients).
