[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m model_response Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Leha like all kinds of strange things. Recently he liked the function F(n, k). Consider all possible k-element subsets of the set [1, 2, ..., n]. For subset find minimal element in it. F(n, k) — mathematical expectation of the minimal element among all k-element subsets.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m But only function does not interest him. He wants to do interesting things with it. Mom brought him two arrays A and B, each consists of m integers. For all i, j such that 1 ≤ i, j ≤ m the condition Ai ≥ Bj holds. Help Leha rearrange the numbers in the array A so that the sum <image> is maximally possible, where A' is already rearranged array.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m First line of input data contains single integer m (1 ≤ m ≤ 2·105) — length of arrays A and B.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Next line contains m integers a1, a2, ..., am (1 ≤ ai ≤ 109) — array A.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Next line contains m integers b1, b2, ..., bm (1 ≤ bi ≤ 109) — array B.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Output m integers a'1, a'2, ..., a'm — array A' which is permutation of the array A.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Examples
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 5
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 7 3 5 3 4
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 2 1 3 2 3
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 4 7 3 5 3
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 7
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 4 6 5 8 8 2 6
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 2 1 2 2 1 1 2
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 2 6 4 5 8 8 6
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m afterremove def solve():
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     m = int(input())
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     a = list(map(int, input().split()))
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     b = list(map(int, input().split())) 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     # Sort the arrays in ascending order 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     a.sort()
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     b.sort() 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     # Initialize the sum to 0 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     for i in range(m): 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m         # Update the sum with the current element 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m         if b[i] < a[i]: 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m             # Swap the current element with the smallest element 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m             a[i], b[i] = b[i], a[i] 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m   
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m     # Return the rearranged array 
