[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m model_response Solve the following coding problem using the programming language python:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Dark  with his love for the prime numbers wanted to do some arithmetic so he decided to do some additions.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m He wants to generate all prime numbers between two given numbers and add them up and decide whether that addition of numbers is a prime number or not?
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Confused, Simply print "YES"(without quotes) if the sum of prime numbers between two numbers is a prime number and print "NO"(without quotes) if the sum of prime numbers between two numbers is a non-prime number.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m Note:
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m If there are no prime numbers between two given numbers print "NO" (without quotes).
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218554)[0m 
