[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m You have unlimited number of coins with values $1, 2, \ldots, n$. You want to select some set of coins having the total value of $S$. 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m It is allowed to have multiple coins with the same value in the set. What is the minimum number of coins required to get sum $S$?
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m The only line of the input contains two integers $n$ and $S$ ($1 \le n \le 100\,000$, $1 \le S \le 10^9$)
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m Print exactly one integer — the minimum number of coins required to obtain sum $S$.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 5 11
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 3
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 6 16
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 3
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m -----Note-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m In the first example, some of the possible ways to get sum $11$ with $3$ coins are: 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m   $(3, 4, 4)$
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m  $(2, 4, 5)$
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m  $(1, 5, 5)$
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m  $(3, 3, 5)$ 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m It is impossible to get sum $11$ with less than $3$ coins.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m In the second example, some of the possible ways to get sum $16$ with $3$ coins are: 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m   $(5, 5, 6)$
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m  $(4, 6, 6)$ 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m It is impossible to get sum $16$ with less than $3$ coins.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m     n, S = map(int, input().split()) 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m   
