[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m Asmany strings are strings of '0's and '1's that have as many 00 as 11. A string such as 00110001 consists of 3 "00" and
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 1 "11". Of course this is not an Asmany string. 0011, 1100, 000111000111 are Asmany strings. An L'th Asmany number is the number of
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m Asmany strings of length L for all positive integers L.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m For esoteric purposes Chef had an oracle (a device) that was capable of answering whether a number that he entered was an Asmany number.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m The problem is that his oracle takes too long for large numbers. Him being Chef, he wants to ask the oracle very
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m large numbers! You tell him that you can give him a better oracle (a program) that will tell him what he wants to know in the blink of
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m an eye.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m ------ Input ------ 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
