[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m model_response For an array a of integers let's denote its maximal element as max(a), and minimal as min(a). We will call an array a of k integers interesting if max(a) - min(a) ≥ k. For example, array [1, 3, 4, 3] isn't interesting as max(a) - min(a) = 4 - 1 = 3 < 4 while array [7, 3, 0, 4, 3] is as max(a) - min(a) = 7 - 0 = 7 ≥ 5.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m You are given an array a of n integers. Find some interesting nonempty subarray of a, or tell that it doesn't exist.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218550)[0m An array b is a subarray of an array a if b can be obtained from a by deletion of several (possibly, zero or all) elements from the beginning and several (possibly, zero or all) elements from the end. In particular, an array is a subarray of itself.
