[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m We have a tree with N vertices numbered 1 to N.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m The i-th edge in this tree connects Vertex a_i and Vertex b_i.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m Consider painting each of these edges white or black. There are 2^{N-1} such ways to paint the edges. Among them, how many satisfy all of the following M restrictions?  
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m  - The i-th (1 \leq i \leq M) restriction is represented by two integers u_i and v_i, which mean that the path connecting Vertex u_i and Vertex v_i must contain at least one edge painted black.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m -----Constraints-----
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m  - 2 \leq N \leq 50
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m  - 1 \leq a_i,b_i \leq N
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m  - The graph given in input is a tree.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m  - 1 \leq M \leq \min(20,\frac{N(N-1)}{2})
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m  - 1 \leq u_i < v_i \leq N
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m  - If i \not= j, either u_i \not=u_j or v_i\not=v_j
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m  - All values in input are integers.
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m 
[36m(WorkerDict pid=218256)[0m -----Input-----
